# Copy this file to .env and set the path to the YeaZ weights you downloaded.
# The pipeline cannot find the weights without it, and segmentation stops with a
# FileNotFoundError naming the path it tried.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# and then edit the path below, or generate it in place from the repository root:
#
#   echo "WEIGHTS_YEAST=$(pwd)/weights/<the-file-you-downloaded>" > .env
#
# Any YeaZ UNet checkpoint loads here. See the README for the download links to
# the published weights; the bright-field ones are the place to start, since the
# movies this pipeline was developed on are bright-field.
#
# The results reported by the authors used a bright-field model from an
# unpublished multi-laboratory YeaZ retraining effort, which is not ours to
# redistribute. Your segmentation quality will differ. `retrain/` has the
# workflow for fine-tuning a checkpoint on your own imaging condition.

WEIGHTS_YEAST=/absolute/path/to/weights/your_yeaz_weights
